H=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;D=H/"data";R=H/"reports";C={x["paper_id"]:x for x in json.loads((D/"interspeech-2025-twentythird-d3-papers.json").read_text())["papers"]};P={x["paper_id"]:x for x in json.loads((D/"interspeech-2025-papers.json").read_text())["papers"]}
N={
"bodur25_interspeech":("Spontaneous speech becomes shorter and less distinct when people speak quickly, so a system or scientist must connect timing to the shape of the vowel space.","Reduction is not one event: speakers can centralize vowels, compress time, or do both, and a global measure may hide that interaction.","Use articulation rate or vowel-space size alone as a complete explanation.","Model spatial vowel distinctiveness and temporal rate together and test whether their interaction predicts non-lexicalized reductions.","French spontaneous speech is measured with pVSA, VDI, articulation rate, and temporally compressed speech zones.","Regression separates spatial predictors, temporal predictors, and their interaction rather than treating one acoustic number as the cause.","Smaller vowel space predicts more reduction only when articulation rate is included; rate is the strongest predictor and VDI is not significant.","The French speakers, spontaneous tasks, reduction definition, and acoustic measures bound the result; other languages and conversational settings remain open."),
"bakkouche25b_interspeech":("A learner must hear and produce an unfamiliar vowel contrast whose important evidence changes over time rather than staying at one frequency point.","Similar categories overlap, and static formant snapshots miss the movement that distinguishes them.","Measure one midpoint formant and treat perception and production as separate abilities.","Track vowel-inherent spectral change across the vowel and compare perception-production alignment with proficiency and immersion experience.","Polish learners produce and perceive English /e-æ/ and /i-I/; dynamic formant movement is measured over vowel duration.","Formant trajectories are time-varying objects; accuracy and production consistency test whether the moving cue is learned.","Advanced learners improve, especially for /i-I/; formant movement increases with proficiency, while length of residence is not significant.","The learner group, contrasts, language experience, and measurements bound the result; other L1s and natural interaction need separate evidence."),
"fernandez25_interspeech":("A streaming system must reconstruct an audio waveform from a magnitude spectrogram without paying a large compute or latency cost.","Magnitude says how much energy is present but not the phase relationships needed to make the waveform line up in time.","Use a large neural inverse model or solve the reconstruction problem with a generic expensive least-squares routine.","Predict phase derivatives with a tiny network and exploit the tridiagonal positive-semidefinite structure of the resulting least-squares system.","The online inversion model uses 8k parameters, adds at most one hop of latency, and applies a linear-complexity solver after predicting derivative information.","Phase reconstruction becomes a structured inverse problem; the solver uses matrix structure instead of treating every coefficient as unrelated.","The paper reports a 30x smaller network, a further halving of neural cost with one-hop latency, and orders-of-magnitude solver speedup while retaining quality.","Spectrogram settings, audio domain, latency definition, and samples bound the claim; listening tests and hardware deployment remain separate checks."),
"charuau25_interspeech":("In a multiparty conversation, gestures and pauses should be understood as timed coordination rather than unrelated events.","A pause can occur within one speaker's turn or between speakers, and gesture timing may reflect planning, turn exchange, or social behavior.","Count gestures and pauses independently or align every gesture only to the nearest word.","Measure gesture category, pause type, duration, and onset/offset timing together in annotated audiovisual dialogues.","MULTISIMO recordings provide multiparty dialogue annotations; distributions and temporal relations are compared for within- and between-speaker pauses.","The unit of analysis is a timed relation among gesture, pause, and speaker turn; duration and onset timing carry different information.","Self-adaptors align with longer pauses, utterance-final syntax shortens pauses, and most gestured pauses occur within utterances.","Corpus annotation, participant population, gesture categories, and observational design bound the result; causal cognitive interpretations remain hypotheses."),
"gong25c_interspeech":("A meeting summarizer should be judged for preserving important facts and staying concise even when no reference summary exists.","Long meetings contain many valid summaries, and reference overlap rewards wording rather than whether the important decisions survived.","Compare generated text with one reference using lexical similarity or ask an LLM for one unstructured score.","Use fact alignment and comparison-based judging, then rank systems with an Elo procedure instead of requiring a reference summary.","CREAM uses reasoning traces and key-fact alignment to compare meeting summaries for completeness and conciseness without references.","Fact coverage and brevity become comparison evidence; Elo aggregates pairwise preferences while avoiding a false absolute scale.","The paper presents a reference-free evaluation framework for meeting summarization and reports its ability to rank systems/prompts.","Facts, judge prompts, meeting domain, and pairwise comparison protocol bound the result; human validation and adversarial summaries remain open."),
"hu25l_interspeech":("A speech-quality or emotion model should account for the fact that listeners use different personal rating scales.","Averaging ordinal ratings can invent distances and erase systematic listener differences.","Average all ratings into one target and train a model to reproduce that mean.","Learn a unified listener scale from pairwise comparisons so the ordering of utterances is preserved without assuming numeric distances.","The method is evaluated on speech quality assessment and continuous emotion recognition, comparing a unified comparison-based scale with mean-listener and multi-scale approaches.","Pairwise comparison models order utterances; the central mathematical choice is to preserve ordinal relationships rather than average incompatible numbers.","The paper reports improved prediction performance and robustness on both tasks.","Listener panels, rating prompts, comparison construction, and datasets bound the result; agreement and usefulness for new listener populations remain open."),
"janse25_interspeech":("A system should predict how hard it is to listen to speech in noise, not merely whether the speech is technically intelligible.","Listeners can reconstruct words by effort even when masking leaves only intermittent speech glimpses, and speaking style changes those glimpses.","Use one global SNR or intelligibility score as a proxy for effort.","Measure high-energy speech glimpses and add speaking-style cues such as pitch range and articulation rate to predict listener effort.","HEGP is computed for habitual and clear-Lombard speech in noise; listening-effort ratings are modeled with spectral balance, F0, and rate measures.","The target is subjective effort, while HEGP is a release-from-masking proxy; regression tests whether style explains residual variance.","HEGP predicts effort similarly across styles; wider F0 range and slower articulation are associated with lower effort, especially for habitual speech.","Noise, listener ratings, speech styles, and HEGP definition bound the result; individual strategy and real device conditions remain open."),
"hou25_interspeech":("Contextual ASR should recognize a large list of names or domain words without being distracted by irrelevant entries.","A large bias list creates search competition and homophone errors, so adding every candidate can hurt the very words it is meant to help.","Pass the full list to decoding or choose entries by frequency alone.","Train a scorer that ranks and selects bias words from an NER-derived list before contextual Whisper decoding.","A bias-word ranking network selects candidates from the IS21 list and evaluates contextual Whisper on LibriSpeech.","Selection turns a huge candidate set into a focused conditional recognition problem; biased WER measures the targeted words while overall WER checks collateral damage.","The paper reports more than 40% relative reduction in biased WER from ranking and selection.","NER list, LibriSpeech, Whisper context mechanism, and bias-word definition bound the result; new domains and errors in entity extraction remain open."),
}
